# =============================================================================
# Release-anchor reconciliation cron (NFM-4452 / ADR-015 §2)
# =============================================================================
# Host-side fallback for the CI `tag-released` job: reads the G4a deploy
# manifest and pushes the `released/<UTCdate>-<sha8>` anchor tag when CI
# could not (GFW egress flake, pre-ADR-015 deploy, manual deploy). Safe on
# every tick: idempotent (already-anchored = exit 0, silent), never moves or
# deletes an existing tag (tag conflict = exit 4 = alarm worth reading),
# skips non-main live SHAs (a rollback is in progress). See
# docs/runbooks/prod-deploy.md §10 and docs/adr/ADR-015-NFM-4452-*.
#
# Exit-code semantics (only non-zero produces output, except conflicts):
#   0 ok / already anchored (silent)   2 manifest missing/invalid
#   3 live SHA not on origin/main      4 TAG CONFLICT — investigate NOW
#   5 push/fetch failed (retry next tick)   6 config error
#
# >>>>> INSTALLATION REQUIRED <<<<<
#
# Deploy-host default paths are filled in below. Adjust REPO_DIR if the
# checkout lives elsewhere.
#
#   Linux (deploy host, root crontab / /etc/cron.d):
#     sudo install -m 0644 scripts/cron/released-anchor-reconcile.cron \
#       /etc/cron.d/nucpot-released-anchor
#
#   macOS (current dev machine, per-user crontab):
#     crontab scripts/cron/released-anchor-reconcile.cron
#     (then strip the `root` user field from the cron line — see below)
#
# =============================================================================

REPO_DIR=/Users/lwj04/Projects/nucpot
PYTHON=/usr/bin/python3

# Every 15 min, offset from the 5-min drift checker. On /etc/cron.d keep the
# `root` user field; in a per-user crontab remove `root`.
*/15 * * * * root cd "$REPO_DIR" && $PYTHON scripts/tag_released.py 2>&1 | grep -v '^already anchored' || true
